 <div class="intro-card searchable" id="start">
  <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-compass" style="color:#2563eb"></i> Start here: the safest way to use the panel</h2>
  <p>This help page explains the visible features and normal admin workflows. Exact access, saving, publishing and approval results still depend on the live Firebase/database rules, storage configuration and the permissions assigned to your account.</p>
  <div class="grid2">
   <div class="mini"><h3>Before you start</h3><p>Use your own approved admin login, check your internet connection, and make sure you are in the correct section before editing or deleting anything.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>After every important action</h3><p>Wait for the success/error message, refresh the relevant list, and confirm the new record is visible. A button click alone does not prove data was saved.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>Publish vs save draft</h3><p>Drafts are for preparing content. Publish/submit actions are intended to make content available or send it into the next workflow; check the resulting status.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>Protect student data</h3><p>Do not share passwords, OTPs, private payment details or screenshots containing student personal information in public groups.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout warn"><strong>Important:</strong> This is a guide to the controls in the admin panel, not a guarantee that a cloud operation succeeded. If Firebase shows <b>PERMISSION_DENIED</b>, network errors or missing configuration, fix the underlying permission/configuration before retrying.</div>
 </div>

 <section class="section searchable" id="login">
  <h2><span class="num">01</span> Login, access request and account safety</h2>
  <p>The admin entry screen includes Login and Request options. Login is for an account that already has admin access. Request is for submitting an access request if the panel offers that workflow; it does not necessarily grant permission automatically.</p>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Open the admin panel</strong><span>Use the official admin page or the app's admin entry point. Check the page address before entering credentials.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Enter the registered admin email and password</strong><span>Use the account that was approved for this panel. Passwords are case-sensitive.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Choose Login to Dashboard</strong><span>Wait for authentication and the saved-session check to finish. Do not click repeatedly while the loader is running.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>If access is not active, use Request or contact the Founder</strong><span>Share the error text and the email used to log in. Never send your password or OTP.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <h3>Common login messages</h3>
  <ul><li><b>Invalid email/password:</b> re-check spelling, keyboard language, Caps Lock and the correct account.</li><li><b>Permission denied / not an admin:</b> authentication may have succeeded, but the database/admin role may not permit access. Ask the Founder to verify your role and database rules.</li><li><b>Page stays loading:</b> reload once, check internet, disable a conflicting extension and try the official URL in a current browser.</li><li><b>Session restored:</b> the browser may have retained an authenticated session. Confirm the displayed admin identity before making changes.</li></ul>
  <div class="callout"><b>Security rule:</b> Never copy an admin's UID, private credentials or privileged database rules into public chats. A public-facing Help Center should never contain passwords, API secrets or private Firebase credentials.</div>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="home">
  <h2><span class="num">02</span> Home dashboard: what each area means</h2>
  <p>The Home area is the admin's overview. It contains welcome/profile information, certificate status or review actions, ranking information, the 14-Day Activity Dashboard, uploaded-content summaries and shortcuts into management sections.</p>
  <div class="grid2">
   <div class="mini"><h3>Welcome / Admin identity</h3><p>Confirms which account is currently open. If the name or account looks wrong, stop and sign out before continuing.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>Certificate status / Review</h3><p>Shows the certificate-related status available to your account. Review opens the certificate workflow where enabled. Eligibility and final status depend on the system's rules.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>Your Uploaded / All Uploaded</h3><p>These summaries help you inspect your own contributions and the broader content list. Use “See All” to open the related list if available.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>Manage Content shortcuts</h3><p>Shortcuts such as News, Blogs, Books, Test Series, Admin Rank and Important Questions take you to the relevant management area.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>Coupon card</h3><p>Shows a Founder-assigned coupon when one is available. Copy/share the correct code and use “Your Code Users” to inspect the coupon-use view.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>App / Return to App</h3><p>Returns to the student-facing app when the route is configured. Use the admin panel's own navigation to come back rather than opening duplicate tabs unnecessarily.</p></div>
  </div>
  <h3>Good daily routine</h3>
  <ol><li>Check the dashboard and activity status.</li><li>Open the content area you need and check existing records first.</li><li>Create or edit one item at a time.</li><li>Wait for the save/publish confirmation.</li><li>Refresh the list and verify the saved item.</li><li>Log out on shared/public devices.</li></ol>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="activity">
  <h2><span class="num">03</span> 14-Day Activity Dashboard</h2>
  <p>This area is intended to help monitor admin contribution activity. In the current panel design, uploaded activity may be represented by calendar/day indicators, including green for a recorded upload day and red for a day without a recorded upload. The dashboard's exact colors, day-count logic and enforcement depend on the live implementation and Firebase rules.</p>
  <div class="grid2">
   <div class="mini"><h3><span class="tag green">Green day</span></h3><p>Typically means an upload/activity record exists for that date. Refresh the dashboard and confirm the content itself is visible.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3><span class="tag red">Red day</span></h3><p>Typically means no qualifying upload has been recorded for that date. It does not by itself prove that an upload failed; check the activity record and content list.</p></div>
  </div>
  <h3>How to record a qualifying activity</h3>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Upload content through a supported admin workflow</strong><span>For example, publish a news item, publish a blog or add a book if those actions are configured as qualifying activity.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Wait for the success message</strong><span>If an error appears, note the exact text. Do not assume activity was counted just because the form closed.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Refresh the content list and activity dashboard</strong><span>Confirm both the content record and the activity date appear, if the feature tracks that action.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>If the day stays red, investigate the data path</strong><span>Check Firebase rules, the admin UID, the expected activity path, the browser console and whether that upload type is wired to activity tracking.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout warn"><b>14-day policy caution:</b> A dashboard indicator is not the same thing as a secure account lock. Client-side HTML alone cannot reliably enforce an account-wide inactivity restriction against a determined user. If a 14-day lock/deactivation is a real access policy, it should be enforced by trusted server-side code or secure database rules, with a clear Founder exemption if intended. Never delete uploaded content as a side effect of an inactivity check.</div>
  <h3>Activity not saving: quick checks</h3>
  <ul><li>Verify the admin is authenticated and the UID is the expected one.</li><li>Check the database for the exact activity node used by the deployed HTML.</li><li>Look for <code>PERMISSION_DENIED</code>, network errors or a rejected promise.</li><li>Ensure the content action actually completed successfully before activity is written.</li><li>Check whether the date uses local time or UTC; uploads near midnight can appear under a neighboring date if time zones differ.</li><li>Do not grant broad public write access just to silence a permission error.</li></ul>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="news">
  <h2><span class="num">04</span> News & Notices: publish updates for students</h2>
  <p>Use News for notices, result announcements, exam updates, admit-card information, deadlines and other time-sensitive information. The editor supports a title, description/content, category, publish status, thumbnail image or image URL, PDF/document and an external link.</p>
  <h3>Step-by-step workflow</h3>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Open News</strong><span>Use the Home shortcut or the News navigation/tab.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Enter a clear title and complete description</strong><span>Include the important date, who the notice applies to, instructions and the official source where appropriate. Use H2/H3 formatting to organize longer content.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Choose a category and publish status</strong><span>Choose the category that best describes the notice. Check whether you intend to publish immediately or keep it in a non-public status.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Add supporting files or links</strong><span>Upload a thumbnail or supply an image URL. Attach a PDF/document or an external link when needed. Avoid adding several conflicting sources.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Publish News and verify</strong><span>Wait for the result message, then inspect Published News/Database Records and refresh. Open the student-facing page to confirm formatting and links.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <h3>Editing and deleting</h3>
  <p>Use the relevant record controls in the published list. Before deleting, verify the title and record carefully. If editing is not offered for a record, use the supported replacement/update workflow rather than modifying unrelated records.</p>
  <div class="callout warn"><b>Common failure:</b> A PDF/image link may be valid text but point to a private, expired or inaccessible file. Test the link in a private browser window or another signed-out browser before publishing.</div>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="blogs">
  <h2><span class="num">05</span> Blog Studio: create learning articles</h2>
  <p>Use Blog Studio for longer educational articles, study guidance, engineering explanations and evergreen learning content. The editor contains blog title, category, author designation, blog content/HTML content, thumbnail or image URL and an optional external link.</p>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Open Blog</strong><span>Choose Blog from Home or the navigation switcher.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Fill in title, category and author designation</strong><span>Use a specific title and the correct category so students can identify the topic.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Write and format the article</strong><span>Use headings, short paragraphs, examples and clear technical terminology. If using the HTML field, ensure the markup is valid and does not contain unsafe scripts.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Add a thumbnail and optional link</strong><span>Use an image you have permission to publish. Check that the image loads and the external link points to the intended resource.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Publish Blog and verify</strong><span>Check Published Blogs, refresh, and open the published article to confirm the layout on mobile.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <p><b>Best practice:</b> Keep the article original, proofread names/dates, avoid copying copyrighted books in full, and never paste private student information into a public blog.</p>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="books">
  <h2><span class="num">06</span> Books Admin: manage books and PDF resources</h2>
  <p>The Books area includes an Add Book form and a Books List. Depending on the form, a book can use a title, category, PDF link or uploaded PDF, thumbnail upload or thumbnail image link.</p>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Open Books and choose Add Book</strong><span>Use Refresh All Books first if you need to check for an existing copy.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Enter the book title and category</strong><span>Use the exact subject/semester or resource category where applicable. Avoid vague titles such as “PDF 1”.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Provide the PDF source</strong><span>Either paste a working PDF link or upload the PDF if the uploader is configured. Follow the form's “OR” instructions rather than assuming both are required.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Add a thumbnail</strong><span>Upload an image or provide a working image link. Use a readable cover image and avoid oversized files.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Save/Add Book(s) and verify</strong><span>Wait for confirmation, refresh the Books List, and open the student-facing book to test the PDF.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <h3>Book upload checklist</h3>
  <ul><li>The PDF opens without requiring your private admin login.</li><li>The title and category match the document.</li><li>The file is not corrupt or empty.</li><li>The thumbnail is visible and appropriate.</li><li>Duplicate entries are avoided by checking the list before adding.</li></ul>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="tests">
  <h2><span class="num">07</span> Test Series: create, preview, draft and publish</h2>
  <p>The Test Series editor includes folder details, test metadata, an MCQ input area, question preview, auto-generated test data and an existing-test list. It also provides a bulk subject/unit workflow.</p>
  <h3>A. Create a single test</h3>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Open Test Series</strong><span>Use the Test Series shortcut or the TEST tab/switcher.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Fill the test metadata</strong><span>Set test title, category, semester, subject, topic, duration, marks per question, negative marking, pass percentage, description and instructions as appropriate. Folder name is optional where marked.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Paste MCQs into MCQ Input</strong><span>Use the expected question format. The Load Sample button can help you inspect the format accepted by the parser.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Choose AUTO GENERATE</strong><span>Review the parsed question preview and generated data. Correct missing options, answer keys, numbering or malformed questions before saving.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Save Draft or Generate & Publish</strong><span>Use Save Draft to keep work in preparation. Use Generate & Publish only after validating the content and settings.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Refresh Existing Test Series</strong><span>Confirm the test appears with the correct title and metadata. If it is published, test the student-facing start flow where possible.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <h3>B. Bulk upload by subjects and units</h3>
  <ol><li>Prepare the input using the subject/unit structure expected by the bulk parser.</li><li>Click <b>SPLIT ALL SUBJECTS & UNITS</b> and inspect the generated separation.</li><li>Review each generated test carefully; bulk parsing can misread inconsistent headings.</li><li>Use <b>SAVE ALL AS DRAFT</b> to review before publishing, or <b>PUBLISH ALL</b> only when every item is correct.</li></ol>
  <h3>C. Test Series quality checklist</h3>
  <ul><li>Question count matches the actual MCQs.</li><li>Every question has one intended correct answer and all options are present.</li><li>Duration, marks and negative marking are correct.</li><li>Pass percentage and instructions are appropriate.</li><li>Hindi/English text and mathematical symbols render correctly.</li><li>Student view starts and completes the test as expected.</li></ul>
  <div class="callout warn"><b>Publishing is consequential:</b> Check answer keys and scoring settings before publishing. If students have already attempted a test, changing its questions or scoring may affect their experience or historical analysis.</div>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="questions">
  <h2><span class="num">08</span> Important Questions Manager</h2>
  <p>This section is for subject-wise important-question sheets. The form includes branch selection, subject, semester, visibility, question content and a unit-wise editor. Hindi and English content are supported in the editor.</p>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Select New / Clear Form</strong><span>Start a fresh sheet instead of accidentally overwriting a previous selection.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Choose branch, subject and semester</strong><span>Double-check the branch and subject before entering content. Visibility determines who should be able to see the sheet according to the app's rules.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Enter Questions Content</strong><span>Organize questions by unit and include clear numbering. Avoid mixing two subjects in one sheet unless the intended format explicitly supports it.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Use Unit-wise Editor if needed</strong><span>Edit unit titles/questions separately, then click Apply Unit Edits to Content so the editor's changes are reflected in the main content field.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Save Sheet and verify</strong><span>Refresh Saved Sheets and confirm the new sheet appears with the right branch, subject and semester.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <p><b>Refresh Saved Sheets</b> reloads the saved list; it is not the same as saving unsaved changes. Copy important text before navigating away from a long form.</p>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="courses">
  <h2><span class="num">09</span> Course Management: create courses and add content</h2>
  <p>Course Management includes Course Creation, Manage Courses and Approvals. A course can have a thumbnail/banner, optional payment QR, title, branch/category, semester/year, fee, included semesters, subject list and description. A course may need approval before students can access it.</p>
  <h3>A. Create a course</h3>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Open Course Management → Course Creation</strong><span>Check Manage Courses first to avoid making a duplicate course.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Add the course identity</strong><span>Enter a clear title, branch/category and primary semester/year. Choose Common only if the course should be available across all branches according to the app's design.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Set fee, semesters and subjects</strong><span>Enter the correct fee, select every semester included in the purchase, and list all subject names one per line if the form requests them. These choices can affect the later content upload selectors.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Add description and images</strong><span>Explain what the course includes. Upload the banner/thumbnail and, if applicable, the payment QR intended for that course.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Save Draft or Save Course for Approval</strong><span>Use the draft action for unfinished work. Submit for approval only after reviewing course title, fee, semester access and description.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Confirm the course status</strong><span>Refresh the catalog/Manage Courses and check whether the course is draft, pending, verified or rejected.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <h3>B. Add video/PDF content to a course</h3>
  <ol><li>Open the intended course from Manage Courses.</li><li>Use Add Video / PDF to This Course.</li><li>Select the semester and subject; if the interface offers a new subject field, use it only when necessary.</li><li>Enter an optional folder/unit name and choose Video or PDF.</li><li>For video, enter a clear title and working video link. For PDF, provide a PDF link or upload a PDF file as supported, with a clear title.</li><li>Click Add to Course, then refresh Course Folders & Content to verify the item.</li></ol>
  <h3>Course safety checklist</h3>
  <ul><li>Test the video/PDF link from a student session or signed-out browser.</li><li>Check that content is attached to the correct course, semester and subject.</li><li>Verify price and payment QR before students make payments.</li><li>Do not promise access until the purchase/approval workflow has been tested.</li><li>Do not delete a course or content item unless you understand the effect on enrolled students.</li></ul>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="approvals">
  <h2><span class="num">10</span> Course payment requests and approval workflow</h2>
  <p>The Course Approval Admin view groups requests by Pending, Verified, Rejected and All. A request can show the student identity, course, amount and payment reference such as UTR. Review the submitted details before taking action.</p>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Open Approvals and refresh</strong><span>Refresh the list so you are reviewing the latest requests.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Open a pending request</strong><span>Match the student, course, fee and transaction reference. Do not approve based only on a screenshot if the payment has not been verified through the accepted process.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Approve only after verification</strong><span>Use the approve/verified action only when payment and request details match. This may unlock course access depending on the backend logic.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Reject with a clear reason when available</strong><span>Use rejection only for a real issue such as a mismatched reference or invalid request. If the reason field is not present, communicate the reason through the official support route.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Refresh and verify the final status</strong><span>Confirm the request moved to the correct status. If the action fails, record the exact error and avoid repeatedly submitting it.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout warn"><b>If Approve/Reject fails:</b> check authentication, request ownership, Firebase Rules for the payment-request node and any course-access node, and browser console errors. Do not “fix” it by making all database writes public. A rejected status should not be treated as proof that money was refunded.</div>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="coupons">
  <h2><span class="num">11</span> Founder-assigned coupon codes, sharing and usage</h2>
  <p>The Home coupon card can show the code assigned to the admin by the Founder, with actions such as Copy Options, Share Coupon and Your Code Users. The Coupon Management area also includes student coupon usage and coupon refresh/copy/share controls where enabled. Founder-level coupon creation/assignment controls may be visible only to authorized roles.</p>
  <h3>A. Share your assigned coupon</h3>
  <div class="steps">
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Locate the Founder-assigned coupon card</strong><span>Check the displayed code carefully. If no code is shown, refresh the panel and ask the Founder to confirm assignment and visibility.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Use Copy Options</strong><span>Choose the copy option provided by the interface and paste the copied text into a message to verify that the code and terms are correct.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Use Share Coupon</strong><span>If browser/device sharing is supported, select the destination app. If sharing is unavailable, copy the code and share it manually.</span></div></div>
   <div class="step"><div><strong>Use Your Code Users</strong><span>Open the usage view to inspect students recorded against your code, where the account has permission to see that information.</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <h3>B. Coupon Management / Founder controls</h3>
  <ul><li><b>Refresh:</b> reloads coupon/usage records from the data source.</li><li><b>Copy Code / Share Code:</b> copies or shares the selected coupon when supported.</li><li><b>Create Coupon for Another Name / Coupon Code / QR:</b> authorized Founder workflows may create a code identity, assign a code and attach a QR image.</li><li><b>Add to This Course / Attach Existing Coupon:</b> associates a saved coupon with the selected course if the interface permits it.</li><li><b>Delete Coupon Code:</b> removes a coupon record only if the account has delete permission. Deletion may affect future use; check carefully before confirming.</li><li><b>All Coupon Codes / Students Who Used a Coupon:</b> offers a broader usage view where permissions allow.</li></ul>
  <div class="callout warn"><b>Coupon errors:</b> “Firebase is not initialized” usually points to initialization/loading order or an unavailable Firebase instance. “Delete failed / permission missing” points to a missing or denied write permission, wrong database path, or an account that is not authorized to delete. Do not open write access to everyone as a workaround.</div>
  <h3>Coupon sharing checklist</h3>
  <ul><li>Share only the code assigned to you or explicitly approved for sharing.</li><li>Do not promise a discount amount unless it matches the live coupon terms.</li><li>Do not alter the code when copying it; watch for spaces or extra punctuation.</li><li>If usage is not updating, refresh and verify the student's purchase/application completed successfully.</li></ul>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="profile">
  <h2><span class="num">12</span> Admin profile, public profile card and ranking</h2>
  <p>The Profile area can contain a profile photo, full name, designation, experience, engineering branch, diploma college, B.Tech college, mobile, address, About text and social/contact links. The interface also includes saved-profile, profile preview/share and admin ranking features.</p>
  <h3>Update your profile</h3>
  <ol><li>Open Profile and choose Edit Profile.</li><li>Fill required fields marked with an asterisk, and check branch/college spelling.</li><li>Upload a suitable profile photo; use Remove only if you intend to remove it.</li><li>Add only social links you control and want publicly displayed. Verify email and phone details before saving.</li><li>Click Save Profile and wait for confirmation.</li><li>Use See Your Profile or the preview to check the saved result. Use Share Profile Card only after reviewing public information.</li></ol>
  <h3>Ranking</h3>
  <p>Admin Ranking displays ranking-related information based on the system's stored data and scoring rules. Refresh Ranking reloads the current list. A rank or score can change as records update; it is not necessarily an immediate reflection of a single upload.</p>
  <div class="callout warn">Treat profile address, mobile number and contact links as public if the profile page can be viewed by students. Do not enter sensitive personal information unless it is necessary and intentionally public.</div>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="app">
  <h2><span class="num">13</span> Navigation, app view and switching sections</h2>
  <p>The panel contains Home, News, Blog, Books, Course, Profile and other content tools. Some screens use a mode switcher (for example NEWS, BLOGS, BOOKS, TEST, COURSE and RANKING); others open a separate form or modal.</p>
  <div class="grid2">
   <div class="mini"><h3>Use tabs to change sections</h3><p>Click the visible tab once and wait for the section to load. If the content does not change, refresh the page once and check the browser console.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>Back / Close buttons</h3><p>Use the screen's own Back or Close control when possible. Some controls close a modal; others return to a list. A browser Back action may leave the admin page.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>Refresh buttons</h3><p>Refresh reloads the list/data shown in that section; it usually does not save the unsaved form currently being edited.</p></div>
   <div class="mini"><h3>Clear / Reset buttons</h3><p>Clear or Reset typically empties the current form. Copy long content first if you have not saved it.</p></div>
  </div>
  <h3>Safe navigation habit</h3>
  <p>Before switching sections, check whether you have unsaved edits. If a form has no draft/auto-save indication, assume your text may be lost when you leave it.</p>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="troubleshooting">
  <h2><span class="num">14</span> Troubleshooting: diagnose before retrying</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Problem / message</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead><tbody>
   <tr><td>Save or Publish does nothing</td><td>Validation error, missing required field, JavaScript error, network issue</td><td>Check required fields, scroll for an error message, wait for the response, then inspect browser console/network if available.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>PERMISSION_DENIED</td><td>Firebase Rules reject this user's read/write at that database path</td><td>Confirm login UID and admin role; ask the Firebase owner to review the exact path and least-privilege rules.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Firebase is not initialized</td><td>Firebase SDK/config is unavailable at the time the action runs, or a module uses a different instance</td><td>Reload the official page, check configuration and script load order, and make sure the correct Firebase project is being used.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Upload fails but form looks filled</td><td>Storage permission, file too large/type unsupported, expired session or poor connection</td><td>Check allowed file type/size, internet, Storage Rules and the exact error. Try a small test file only if appropriate.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Record saved but not visible</td><td>List not refreshed, wrong category/filter, wrong database path, status is draft/pending</td><td>Refresh the list, clear filters, check status and verify you are in the same Firebase project.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Coupon copy/share fails</td><td>Clipboard/share API blocked or browser/device does not support it</td><td>Try HTTPS in a modern browser; use the manual fallback if the interface offers one.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Approve/reject fails</td><td>Missing permission, request path mismatch, expired auth session or status already changed</td><td>Refresh approvals, reopen the request, verify status and ask the owner to check rules for the exact node.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>14-day activity remains red</td><td>Upload not counted, activity write failed, date/time mismatch or dashboard not refreshed</td><td>Verify the content record and activity record separately; inspect database rules and the exact error.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Test parser creates wrong questions</td><td>Inconsistent input format, missing answer markers, headings mixed with question text</td><td>Load sample format, normalize numbering/options, generate preview again, and review every answer before publishing.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Student cannot open PDF/video</td><td>Link is private, expired, malformed or not a direct/compatible file link</td><td>Open the URL while signed out, confirm sharing access and replace the link if necessary.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Course not unlocked after approval</td><td>Approval succeeded but entitlement update failed, stale app session, mismatched UID/course ID</td><td>Refresh the request, verify the approved record and purchase/access record, then ask the owner to inspect the unlock logic.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Page is stuck / buttons don't respond</td><td>Script error, stale cached page, browser extension or partial load</td><td>Save/copy unsaved text, reload once, use a current browser, disable interfering extensions and report console errors.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h3>What to include when reporting a bug</h3>
  <ul><li>Which screen and exact button you used.</li><li>What you expected to happen and what actually happened.</li><li>The full error text and approximate time.</li><li>Whether the record appears after refresh.</li><li>Browser/device and whether the same issue happens after signing in again.</li></ul>
  <div class="callout good"><b>Good debugging rule:</b> First check the saved record and error message. Do not repeatedly click Publish, Approve, Reject or Delete; repeated clicks may create duplicates or repeat an action.</div>
 </section>

 <section class="section searchable" id="faq">
  <h2><span class="num">15</span> Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
  <p>Type a word in the search box at the top to filter this guide and these questions. Tap a question to reveal the answer.</p>
  <div class="faq-list" id="faqList">
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>1. I cannot log in. What should I do?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Check the email/password, connection and account used. If the message says not authorized or permission denied, ask the Founder to verify your admin role and the Firebase rules. Never share your password or OTP.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>2. What is the difference between Login and Request?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Login is for an account that already has access. Request is an access-request workflow if enabled; submitting a request does not necessarily grant admin privileges automatically.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>3. How do I know if my content really saved?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Wait for the success message, refresh the relevant list and confirm the record is still present. If possible, open the student-facing page too.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>4. Does Refresh save my form?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Normally no. Refresh reloads the displayed list/data. Save or publish your form first and copy long text before refreshing.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>5. What does PERMISSION_DENIED mean?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The current authenticated account is not permitted to perform that read/write under the database rules, or the code is targeting a path the rules do not allow. The owner should check the exact path and UID.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>6. Why is my upload not counting in the 14-day activity calendar?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The upload may not be a qualifying activity, the activity write may have failed, the date may be stored in a different timezone, or the dashboard may be stale. Verify both the content record and activity record.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>7. Will one red day automatically lock my account?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No conclusion should be drawn from a single color alone. The displayed calendar is an indicator. Any actual 14-day lock policy must be confirmed in the deployed implementation and securely enforced by trusted backend logic/rules.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>8. What if I uploaded something but activity shows no data?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Refresh the content list and dashboard; verify the activity node in Firebase and check for permission/network errors. Report the exact upload type and error rather than making database rules public.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>9. How do I publish a news notice?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Open News, enter the title and content, choose category/status, attach a thumbnail/PDF/link as needed, click Publish News and confirm it appears in Published News after refresh.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>10. Can I use an image URL instead of uploading an image?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Where the form offers “OR Image URL”, yes. Make sure the URL is publicly accessible, loads directly and is not a temporary/private link.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>11. What is the best use of Blog Studio?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use it for longer educational articles and learning resources. Use News for time-sensitive notices. Check the title, author designation, formatting, thumbnail and links before publishing.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>12. My PDF was saved but students cannot open it. Why?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The file may be private, expired, corrupt or incompatible. Open the link while signed out, confirm access permissions and test the file itself.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>13. Should I provide both a PDF link and upload a PDF?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Follow the specific form's instructions. If it says link OR upload, provide one working source unless the interface explicitly asks for both.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>14. How do I create a test without publishing it immediately?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Fill the metadata and MCQs, generate the preview, verify questions/answers, then use Save Draft. Reopen or refresh Existing Test Series to confirm the draft appears.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>15. Why did the test parser split questions incorrectly?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use the format shown by Load Sample, keep numbering/options consistent and ensure answer keys are clearly marked. Generate again and inspect the full preview before publishing.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>16. What is the difference between Save Draft and Publish?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Draft is for work that still needs review. Publish is intended to make the content available or move it into the published workflow. Always verify the resulting status.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>17. How do I upload Important Questions unit-wise?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Select branch, subject and semester, enter the sheet, edit unit titles/questions if needed, click Apply Unit Edits to Content, then Save Sheet and verify in Saved Sheets.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>18. Why are my unit edits missing from the final sheet?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>After editing the unit-wise editor, click Apply Unit Edits to Content before saving. Then verify the main content and saved sheet.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>19. How do I create a course for all branches?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Choose the Common — All Branches category only if that is the intended availability. Review semester access, subject list and description before submitting.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>20. Why can I not select the right semester or subject when uploading course content?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Check that the course includes the semester and that the subject list was entered correctly when the course was created. Refresh the course detail view after correcting course metadata.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>21. How do I add a video or PDF to a course?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Open the course, use Add Video/PDF, choose semester and subject, enter folder/unit and title, provide the video/PDF link or upload as supported, click Add to Course, then refresh Course Folders & Content.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>22. A course is pending. Is it available to students?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Do not assume so. Check the course status and the app's intended approval rules. A pending course may require review before it becomes available.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>23. Why did course approval or rejection fail?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Refresh the request, confirm it has not already changed status, check authentication and ask the database owner to review write permission for the exact request path. Do not loosen all database rules.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>24. Does Reject mean a refund was issued?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No. Rejection changes a request's status according to the app's logic; it does not by itself prove that a payment was refunded.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>25. My Founder-assigned coupon is not visible. What should I check?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Refresh the admin page, confirm you are signed in to the correct account, and ask the Founder to verify that a coupon was assigned to your identity and that you have read permission.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>26. How do Copy Options and Share Coupon differ?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Copy Options copies available coupon text/options to the clipboard. Share Coupon uses the device/browser sharing feature where supported. If sharing is unavailable, copy the code and share it manually.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>27. Why does Your Code Users show no students?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>There may be no recorded usage yet, the usage list may need refreshing, or permissions/data mapping may be incorrect. Verify an actual coupon redemption before assuming a bug.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>28. Coupon delete fails with a permission error. What should I do?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Confirm you have the required Founder/admin role and that rules permit deletion at the exact coupon node. Check the console/error path. Do not make coupon data publicly writable to bypass the error.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>29. How do I update my admin profile?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Open Profile → Edit Profile, fill required fields, update the photo/links, Save Profile, then use the preview or See Your Profile to confirm.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>30. Is my profile information public?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Assume profile details and social/contact links may be visible to students if a public profile page/card is enabled. Only enter information you intend to share publicly.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>31. Why did my ranking not change after uploading?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Ranking may use its own scoring logic and refresh cycle. Refresh Ranking and check the criteria; a single upload may not immediately change rank.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>32. Can I safely delete old content?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Only after confirming the exact record and understanding the effect on student access, course purchases, test attempts and links. Deletion may not be reversible; keep an authorized backup when appropriate.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>33. What should I send to support?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Send the screen name, button, exact error text, time, device/browser and whether the record appears after refresh. Remove passwords, OTPs, payment secrets and unnecessary student personal data from screenshots.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>34. What if the page is stuck or a button does not work?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Copy unsaved text, reload once, try a current browser and check the connection. If it persists, report the exact button and browser console error. Do not repeatedly click destructive actions.</p></div></details>
   <details class="faq-item searchable"><summary>35. How do I leave the admin panel safely?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Use Logout when finished, especially on a shared device. Do not leave an authenticated admin session open on a public computer.</p></div></details>
  </div>
  <div class="no-results" id="noResults">No matching help topics found. Try a shorter term such as “save”, “Firebase”, “course”, “coupon” or “activity”.</div>
 </section>
 <section class="section searchable" id="support">
  <h2><span class="num"><i class="fa-solid fa-life-ring"></i></span> When you need help from the Founder / technical owner</h2>
  <p>Use this checklist to send a useful support report:</p>
  <ol><li>Admin account email or UID only through the approved private channel—never publish it publicly.</li><li>Screen/feature name (News, Books, Test Series, Course Approval, Coupon, Activity, etc.).</li><li>Exact action and error message.</li><li>Whether the record appears after refresh.</li><li>Approximate date/time and device/browser.</li><li>A screenshot with passwords, OTPs, payment details and unrelated student data hidden.</li></ol>
  <div class="callout good"><b>Final rule:</b> Make one change, wait for confirmation, refresh and verify. This simple habit prevents duplicate records and makes technical issues much easier to diagnose.</div>
 </section>
